{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In Elohim and in Moses.</b> They equated the servant to his Master (Tanchuma)." "<b>Why have you brought us up.</b> Both of them are equal." "<b>And our soul is disgusted.</b> This too is a term of constriction of spirit and loathing." "<b>The light bread.</b> Because the manna was absorbed into the limbs, they called it קְלֹקֵל. They said: This manna is destined to swell up in our intestines — is there any creature born of woman who takes in and does not let out? (Yoma 75)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:52.220233150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}